From d093c11753579068cdbf556a629a1152c04b6096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:33:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] trans: MakeDst reads the vtable out of a DynMetadata metadata
 operand

cursive_core 0.3.5 (jlq 0.1.0), in an `Rc<dyn Fn(&mut Cursive)>` method
of alloc::rc:

    libcursive_core-0_3_5.rlib.c:92022:40: error: incompatible type for argument 2 of 'make_traitobjptr'
        var1 = make_traitobjptr(var28, var29);  // _1 = MakeDst(_28, _29)
    note: expected 'void *' but argument is of type 'struct s_..DynMetadata<dyn Fn(&mut Cursive)>..'

1.90's `Rc::from_raw` goes `byte_sub` -> `with_metadata_of` ->
`ptr::from_raw_parts(data, ptr::metadata(meta))`. `ptr_metadata` lowers
to DstMeta and `aggregate_raw_ptr` to MakeDst. For a trait object,
`ptr::metadata` returns `DynMetadata<dyn Trait>` (`_vtable_ptr:
NonNull<VTable>` plus a PhantomData), and the C backend's DstMeta already
stores the vtable into `._0._0` of that struct. MakeDst handed the
metadata operand to make_traitobjptr unchanged, which is only right when
the operand is the vtable pointer itself (unsize coercions, and the
`&VTable` metadata of the pre-1.54 world).

The TraitObject arm now looks at the metadata operand's type: a pointer
or borrow is passed through, anything else must be the DynMetadata struct
and is read back from `._0._0`. Slices and thin pointers are unchanged.
The old output never compiled, so nothing already built is miscompiled.

The shape is generic in `with_metadata_of`, so it only shows up in
a crate that instantiates `Rc`/`Arc`/`Weak::from_raw`, `byte_add`/
`byte_sub` or `with_metadata_of` on a `dyn` pointer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
